codex
Track B does not rescue the proposed relabelling idea. If the relabelling is exposed, producing the conjugated involution is the same short table operation available to the solver; if it is hidden, the solver has no compact structural route and must perform graph-automorphism work on the incidence structure. Either way, all seeds remain one canonical isomorphism class, so the required diversity and scaling gates fail. I’m quantifying those costs and documenting the rejection.
