codex
The paper confirms the earlier note’s facts, but it also exposes a better Track B possibility that the note did not consider: every symmetric design incidence matrix satisfies a two-eigenvalue Gram identity. That makes selected entries of its exact inverse a short rational witness. Generic exact inversion is cubic, while the design identity reduces each requested entry to one incidence lookup. I’m testing whether this can satisfy scaling, diversity, answer-size, and honesty requirements without leaving the paper’s native incidence-matrix objects.
