codex
The Track B escape does not survive the “from this paper” requirement: computing inverse entries or determinants of weighted incidence matrices would introduce a new linear-algebra benchmark not studied or licensed by the paper. For the paper-native tasks, the split is decisive: relabelled existence witnesses are locally checkable but canonically identical and fixed-size; the paper’s substantive completeness claim is expensive to reproduce and has no locally checkable completeness certificate. I’m tightening the rejection note’s cost accounting before finalizing it.
