Rejected at Step 0; no generator was shipped. The decision is documented in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.13722/REJECTED.md).

Key findings from the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13722):

- Relabelling a known design and involution passes G and V, but fails Track A hardness, scaling, and canonical diversity.
- Track B also fails: with the relabelling exposed, the mechanical and compact routes are identical—70 table writes, measured at 12.42 μs per certificate.
- The substantive classification enumerates 18,894 orbit matrices and 11,670,332 intermediate representatives, yielding 11,642,495 classes, but supplies no cheaply checkable completeness certificate.
- Section 3’s general Hadamard extension is explicit and therefore easy; it provides neither a hard search problem nor scalable source designs with involutions.

The rejection records the exact failing gates, both Track A and Track B analysis, mechanical-versus-compact costs, theorem references, and why the obvious repairs are not paper-native.
